  "refetch": "pages at terminal `none`. A re-fetch is a fresh consent resolution per origin (ADR-024/ADR-103) and a fresh capture, not a replay; it cannot be priced from GPU time. Task 579 section 6 declined to price it for the same reason and this register does not either.",
  "chain_adr093": "pages at terminal `l2_only`. Reconstructable by the ratified L1-b overlap chainer at its measured 99.843% chain fidelity / 0.135% material loss; the output must land in l1/, not in a _work tree.",
  "promote_unpromoted_stores": "Independently of the two above: task 581's exhaustive walk (tasks/581-scripts/store_discovery_581.py) found 885,805 url-and-text-bearing files, 405,518,700,363 bytes, under `_work/` - outside every ADR-026 layer, in scratch trees named after tasks. That text is NOT lost, it is unfiled, and no store registry can see it. Promoting it into l1/release=... is the cheapest item on this list and the one that shrinks the other two."
